From 3fc4bcf42b0cbb9604917e32be3b6a20564c73d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: batya <batya@github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:31:04 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] feat(server): sessions and how they play back live in
 the library

A workspace is the studio's session of work: the songs made in it, and whether
it is still open. One is open at a time. Sessions used to live in the window, so
the window and an agent each had their own set; they live in the database now,
with workspace_songs linking tracks the way playlist_songs already does, and the
schema is added with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS so an existing library picks it
up without a migration.

The repeat mode and shuffle are stored per context - a session, a playlist, the
library, a search - so a choice made in one queue does not follow the user into
another. REST routes follow the playlists': list, create, get, rename, delete,
open, close, and reading or writing a context's playback mode.

A session that was only created is closed: open means an empty closed_at, and
creating one used to look like opening it.
